# Shell scripts must check out with LF even on Windows.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the primary dev machine, so without this rule git
# rewrites these files to CRLF on checkout. For a /bin/sh script that is not
# cosmetic: `exit 1\r` makes the shell try to exit with the non-numeric status
# "1\r", and the hook stops blocking anything while still printing its error
# text — a guard that looks like it works and doesn't. (Observed exactly once
# while building .githooks/pre-push; see audit CFG-01.)
*.sh            text eol=lf
.githooks/**    text eol=lf
